3
00:01:19.613 --> 00:01:20.745
LAST CARD.

4
00:01:20.781 --> 00:01:22.246
AN ACE HELPS LOW.

5
00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.748
KING. NO HELP.

6
00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:25.249
5. PAIR UP.

7
00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.751
DEALER GETS 4.

8
00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:28.264
REMEMBER THOSE SWEAT SUITS

9
00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.599
WE SAW FOR 19 BUCKS?

10
00:01:29.623 --> 00:01:31.601
RODBELL'S HAS THEM FOR $14.99.

11
00:01:31.625 --> 00:01:34.592
RODBELL'S IS THE
ONLY PLACE IN AMERICA

12
00:01:34.628 --> 00:01:37.529
WHERE YOU CAN GET
THONGS ALL YEAR ROUND.

13
00:01:37.565 --> 00:01:39.208
DARLENE. YOU DIDN'T ANTE.

14
00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.332
SORRY. DAD.

15
00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.134
WE BET $50.000.

16
00:01:42.169 --> 00:01:43.201
I CALL.

17
00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.936
IT'S NOT YOUR TURN.

18
00:01:44.972 --> 00:01:47.004
YEAH. BUT IT'S MY HOUSE.

19
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.508
WE PLAYING OR
SHOOTING THE BREEZE?

20
00:01:49.543 --> 00:01:51.009
SHOOTING THE BREEZE.

21
00:01:51.045 --> 00:01:52.455
OK. THE PORTCHESTER GAME.

22
00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:54.780
LAST GAME OF MY SENIOR YEAR.

23
00:01:54.815 --> 00:01:56.281
ONE MINUTE TO GO.

24
00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.783
LET'S PLAY POKER.

25
00:01:57.818 --> 00:01:59.128
WE'RE SHOOTING THE BREEZE.

26
00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.419
WE KNOW THIS STORY.

27
00:02:00.454 --> 00:02:02.420
THIS TIME... THE REFEREE'S SIDE.

28
00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.822
I GOT A PAIR.

29
00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.223
SO DO I.

30
00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.225
YEAH. BUT ROSEANNE'S
ARE SHOWING.

31
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.060
YOU THINK WE DON'T GET

32
00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.096
YOUR CORNY LITTLE SEX JOKES.

33
00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:15.233
HEY. YOU KIDS ARE OUR
CORNY LITTLE SEX JOKES.

34
00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:19.237
[DOORBELL RINGS]

35
00:02:19.273 --> 00:02:20.739
CHEESE IT. THE FUZZ.

36
00:02:20.774 --> 00:02:23.074
HIDE THE CARDS AND THE CHIPS.

37
00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:25.910
I THINK IT'S TIME WE TAUGHT D.J.

38
00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.045
HOW TO PLAY 52-CARD PICKUP.

39
00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:31.083
AAH.

40
00:02:31.118 --> 00:02:32.584
TA-DA!

41
00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.920
DAD. WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

42
00:02:34.955 --> 00:02:37.756
I CAME TO SEE MY
SWEET LITTLE KAPUTCHKA.

43
00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:38.868
AL!

44
00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.258
HEY. DANNY.

45
00:02:40.294 --> 00:02:41.759
DAD!

46
00:02:41.795 --> 00:02:43.261
OH. MY GOSH!

47
00:02:43.297 --> 00:02:44.762
IS EVERYTHING OK?

48
00:02:44.798 --> 00:02:45.931
FINE. FINE.

49
00:02:45.966 --> 00:02:47.332
WHERE'S GRANDMA?

50
00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.668
THERE SHE IS NOW.

51
00:02:50.704 --> 00:02:51.870
HELLO.

52
00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.605
MA!

53
00:02:53.641 --> 00:02:56.941
MOM. HI.

54
00:02:56.977 --> 00:02:59.811
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS
DOING IN LANFORD?

55
00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.047
THIS MORNING I ASKED YOUR MOTHER

56
00:03:02.082 --> 00:03:03.882
WHAT SHE WANTED TO DO.

57
00:03:03.918 --> 00:03:06.151
SO WE TOOK A LITTLE RIDE.

58
00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:09.955
250 MILES ISN'T A LITTLE DRIVE.

59
00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:12.390
ESPECIALLY WHEN
YOU HAVE A WOMAN.

60
00:03:12.426 --> 00:03:14.225
WHO WHENEVER A CAR PASSES.

61
00:03:14.261 --> 00:03:16.628
SAYS. "I WONDER
WHERE THEY'RE GOING."

62
00:03:16.664 --> 00:03:18.096
BOY. SHE'S GOT PROBLEMS.

63
00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.576
WHY DIDN'T YOU CALL?

64
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.401
I DID. BUT YOUR LINE WAS BUSY.

65
00:03:22.436 --> 00:03:23.902
I TRIED YOUR SISTER.

66
00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.404
I COULDN'T GET HER.

67
00:03:25.439 --> 00:03:27.906
I THOUGHT MAYBE
SOMETHING WAS WRONG.

68
00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.442
GOD KNOWS SHE'D NEVER TELL ME.

69
00:03:30.477 --> 00:03:33.177
MY APARTMENT'S
GETTING FUMIGATED.

70
00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.746
FUMIGATED FOR WHAT.

71
00:03:34.782 --> 00:03:37.516
THOSE LOUSES YOU GO OUT WITH?

72
00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.922
THEY'RE BACK.

73
00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:54.933
WE NEED MILK?

74
00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.434
WE NEED EGGS?

75
00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:57.736
BULLETS?

76
00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:03.008
COME ON. DAN. LET'S JUST
TRY TO GET THROUGH THIS.

77
00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.044
WHAT ARE YOU DOING UP?

78
00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.546
I CAN'T SLEEP.

79
00:04:07.581 --> 00:04:09.058
GRANDPA'S IN THE BATHROOM

80
00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.560
MAKING THOSE GAGGING NOISES.

81
00:04:10.584 --> 00:04:11.883
EU!

82
00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.385
HOW LONG'S HE BEEN IN THERE?

83
00:04:14.421 --> 00:04:16.433
AT LEAST HALF AN HOUR.

84
00:04:16.457 --> 00:04:19.424
HE'S PROBABLY GOT
IT ALL UP BY NOW.

85
00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.427
WHY DON'T YOU GO BACK TO BED?

86
00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.429
HE'S REALLY DRIVING ME CRAZY.

87
00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.931
IF HE SAYS. "PULL MY FINGER"

88
00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.401
ONE MORE TIME...

89
00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:30.902
WELL. NOW YOU KNOW

90
00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:34.072
WHERE I GET MY SMART.
SOPHISTICATED WIT.

91
00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:37.409
I CAN'T BELIEVE THAT
MAN RAISED YOU.

92
00:04:37.444 --> 00:04:40.912
NOW YOU KNOW WHY I
MARRIED YOU SO YOUNG.

93
00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:42.914
YOU WERE MADLY IN LOVE.

94
00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:46.718
WITH THE IDEA OF
GETTING OUT OF MY HOUSE.

95
00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:50.321
IS THERE A PLACE IN
HERE TO SIT DOWN?

96
00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.324
WHY DON'T YOU TRY
ONE OF THESE THINGS

97
00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.826
WE CALL CHAIRS?

98
00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:58.062
WE SIT IN THEM FREQUENTLY.

99
00:04:58.098 --> 00:05:01.166
WHAT KIND OF LIST IS HE MAKING?

100
00:05:01.201 --> 00:05:02.801
A HIT LIST.

101
00:05:05.572 --> 00:05:08.372
HE'S GOING OUT TO THE STORE.

102
00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.875
DON'T GET ANYTHING
SPECIAL FOR ME.

103
00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.878
BUT YOUR FATHER'S
DIET IS LOW SODIUM.

104
00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:16.647
LOW FAT. AND HIGH FIBER.

105
00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:19.662
WHY DON'T WE JUST
GET HIM SOME WOOD?

106
00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:22.487
HE CAN PUT MUSTARD ON IT.

107
00:05:22.523 --> 00:05:23.988
MUSTARD'S HIGH IN FAT.

108
00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.857
MANY PEOPLE DON'T KNOW THAT.

109
00:05:25.893 --> 00:05:27.570
MANY PEOPLE DON'T CARE.

110
00:05:27.594 --> 00:05:28.727
I DO.

111
00:05:28.762 --> 00:05:31.362
BUT DOGGONE IT. I GOT TO GO.

112
00:05:36.603 --> 00:05:38.570
HE'S NOT WORKING. IS HE?

113
00:05:38.605 --> 00:05:39.771
HE'S WORKING.

114
00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:42.273
I'M GLAD BECAUSE
YOUR FATHER WORRIES.

115
00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:44.388
ESPECIALLY ABOUT YOUR SISTER.

116
00:05:46.613 --> 00:05:48.079
HE DOESN'T HAVE TO WORRY.

117
00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.592
WELL. SOMEBODY HAS TO.

118
00:05:49.616 --> 00:05:50.749
SHE'S 32.

119
00:05:50.784 --> 00:05:51.916
SHE'S UNMARRIED.

120
00:05:51.952 --> 00:05:56.254
HEAVEN FORBID SHE TURNS
OUT TO BE LIKE YOUR AUNT DALE

121
00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:57.622
WHO TEACHES P.E.

122
00:05:57.657 --> 00:06:01.159
SPEAKING OF AUNT DALE.
HOW IS UNCLE SHIRLEY?

123
00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:05.875
ALSO. YOUR FATHER'S CONCERNED

124
00:06:05.899 --> 00:06:08.867
BECAUSE YOUR SISTER
LIVES IN A BUILDING

125
00:06:08.902 --> 00:06:10.880
THAT NEEDS TO BE FUMIGATED.

126
00:06:10.904 --> 00:06:12.370
BUT I'M HER MOTHER.

127
00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:16.307
IT'S NOT MY JOB TO
TELL HER WHAT TO DO.

128
00:06:16.343 --> 00:06:17.809
BUT IT'S YOUR JOB

129
00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:21.345
TO TELL ME TO TELL
HER WHAT TO DO.

130
00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:24.816
YES. I'M SURE PETUNIAS
ARE PERENNIALS.

131
00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.890
JACKIE. MOM WAS JUST
TALKING ABOUT YOU.

132
00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.403
NOW YOU GET TO LISTEN

133
00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:36.528
WHILE SHE TALKS ABOUT ME.

134
00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:42.100
WE GOING TO TALK ABOUT ROSEANNE?

135
00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:43.267
CERTAINLY NOT.

136
00:06:43.303 --> 00:06:46.115
IT'S JUST THAT YOUR
FATHER'S WORRIED ABOUT HER.

137
00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:47.739
SHE SEEMS SO TIRED.

138
00:06:47.774 --> 00:06:51.543
MOM. YOU'VE BEEN HERE A
GRAND TOTAL OF ONE HOUR.

139
00:06:51.578 --> 00:06:54.546
HOW DO YOU KNOW
HOW TIRED SHE IS?

140
00:06:54.581 --> 00:06:56.581
A MOTHER KNOWS.

141
00:06:56.617 --> 00:06:59.083
GRANTED IT WAS A
DIFFERENT GENERATION.

142
00:06:59.119 --> 00:07:01.520
BUT YOUR FATHER WOULD HAVE DIED

143
00:07:01.555 --> 00:07:03.521
BEFORE HE MADE ME WORK.

144
00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:05.857
DAN DOESN'T MAKE ROSEANNE WORK.

145
00:07:05.893 --> 00:07:07.859
THAT'S WHAT SHE TELLS YOU.

146
00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:11.073
YOU'RE NOT MARRIED. YOU
DON'T KNOW THESE THINGS.

147
00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:14.065
WHAT DID YOU FIND OUT ABOUT ME?

148
00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.967
YOU'RE VERY TIRED.

149
00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:18.470
HEY. MA. IS TWO BLANKETS ENOUGH?

150
00:07:18.505 --> 00:07:19.704
TWO'S FINE...

151
00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:22.407
IF THAT'S ALL YOU HAVE.

152
00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:25.276
I HAVE MORE. HOW
MANY WOULD YOU LIKE?

153
00:07:25.312 --> 00:07:27.290
WHAT DID YOUR FATHER SAY?

154
00:07:27.314 --> 00:07:29.280
HE SAYS HE'LL BE SLEEPING

155
00:07:29.316 --> 00:07:30.781
IN THE DRIVEWAY NAKED.

156
00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:33.284
HOW MANY BLANKETS DO YOU WANT?

157
00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.785
IF YOU HAVE TWO.

158
00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:37.355
TWO'S FINE.

159
00:07:43.096 --> 00:07:45.063
I'M CLOSE TO THE EDGE.

160
00:07:45.098 --> 00:07:48.065
IF I GO OVER. YOU'RE
COMING WITH ME.

161
00:07:48.101 --> 00:07:51.069
SHE DOES HAVE A WAY ABOUT HER.

162
00:07:51.104 --> 00:07:53.571
IF SHE WANTS TO RAG ON YOU.

163
00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:56.074
WHY DOESN'T SHE JUST TELL YOU?

164
00:07:56.109 --> 00:07:59.077
I'M SICK OF THESE
BEHIND-THE-BACK CONVERSATIONS.

165
00:07:59.112 --> 00:08:02.025
LIKE THE ONE WE'RE HAVING
ABOUT MOM RIGHT NOW?

166
00:08:02.049 --> 00:08:03.014
YEAH. YEAH.

167
00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:06.517
WHY SHOULD I HAVE TO
DEFEND THE GUYS YOU DATE?

168
00:08:06.553 --> 00:08:07.686
YOU SHOULDN'T.

169
00:08:07.721 --> 00:08:10.689
AND I'M TIRED OF
EXPLAINING TO HER

170
00:08:10.724 --> 00:08:14.325
WHY YOUR HOUSE IS
SO FILTHY ALL THE TIME.

171
00:08:15.562 --> 00:08:17.028
YEAH. THAT'S MY BUSINESS.

172
00:08:17.064 --> 00:08:19.042
SHE JUST DOESN'T LET UP.

173
00:08:19.066 --> 00:08:20.531
SHE'S GOING TO LET UP

174
00:08:20.567 --> 00:08:22.901
BECAUSE I'M GOING
TO LAY INTO HER.

175
00:08:22.936 --> 00:08:25.737
THAT WOMAN'S NOT QUALIFIED
TO JUDGE ANYBODY'S LIFE.

176
00:08:25.772 --> 00:08:27.038
MA?

177
00:08:27.073 --> 00:08:28.551
ENOUGH IS ENOUGH ALREADY.

178
00:08:28.575 --> 00:08:30.575
WE GOT TO DO THIS.

179
00:08:30.611 --> 00:08:33.611
I FOUND THIS UNDER
YOUR SISTER'S SOFA.

180
00:08:33.646 --> 00:08:36.615
MOM. WHY ARE YOU
GIVING IT TO ME?

181
00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:39.284
IT'S HER POTATO CHIPS. HER SOFA.

182
00:08:39.319 --> 00:08:41.786
IF YOU DON'T LIKE THE WAY

183
00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:44.289
ROSEANNE KEEPS
HOUSE. TALK TO ROSEANNE.

184
00:08:44.324 --> 00:08:48.293
IF YOU DON'T LIKE
THE WAY I RUN MY LIFE.

185
00:08:48.328 --> 00:08:51.296
TALK TO ME ABOUT
IT. NOT TO ROSEANNE.

186
00:08:51.331 --> 00:08:54.299
WE'RE SICK OF THE
WAY YOU MANIPULATE US.

187
00:08:54.334 --> 00:08:56.567
IS THAT SO. ROSEANNE?

188
00:09:00.107 --> 00:09:01.239
YEAH.

189
00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:02.574
RIGHT?

190
00:09:02.609 --> 00:09:05.577
WELL. MAYBE MANIPULATE'S
KIND OF A HARSH WORD

191
00:09:05.612 --> 00:09:07.078
TO USE HERE.

192
00:09:07.114 --> 00:09:09.581
I JUST THINK WHAT JACKIE MEANS.

193
00:09:09.616 --> 00:09:11.583
WHAT SHE'S TRYING TO SAY.

194
00:09:11.618 --> 00:09:13.084
IS THAT WE WISH

195
00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:17.088
YOU WOULD DEAL WITH US
IN A MORE DIRECT MANNER.

196
00:09:17.124 --> 00:09:20.103
NO. THAT'S NOT WHAT
JACKIE'S TRYING TO SAY.

197
00:09:20.127 --> 00:09:22.093
WHERE THE HELL WERE YOU

198
00:09:22.129 --> 00:09:24.061
FIVE MINUTES AGO?

199
00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.767
WHERE DO YOU WANT THIS COT?

200
00:09:29.802 --> 00:09:32.781
SET UP ON A BEACH IN CANCUN.

201
00:09:32.805 --> 00:09:34.071
D.J.!

202
00:09:34.107 --> 00:09:35.073
WHAT?

203
00:09:35.108 --> 00:09:37.086
GO UP TO BED NOW.

204
00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:38.609
OK.

205
00:09:38.645 --> 00:09:40.611
I'LL GET SOME SHEETS. MOM.

206
00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:46.150
YOU REALLY SHOULD TURN
YOUR MATTRESS MORE OFTEN.

207
00:09:46.186 --> 00:09:47.518
WHERE WILL YOU SLEEP?

208
00:09:47.554 --> 00:09:49.632
ANYWHERE'S OK WITH ME.

209
00:09:49.656 --> 00:09:51.623
HEY. I DON'T SLEEP ANYWHERE.

210
00:09:51.658 --> 00:09:54.926
HELL. THESE... THESE
COTS ARE PRETTY NICE.

211
00:09:54.962 --> 00:09:57.940
I'M SURE THEY DON'T
WANT TO SLEEP ON COTS.

212
00:09:57.964 --> 00:10:00.364
WHAT DID WE DO LAST TIME?

213
00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:04.502
LAST TIME? I'VE COMPLETELY
BLOCKED IT OUT OF MY MIND.

214
00:10:06.072 --> 00:10:09.040
YOU GUYS DON'T MIND
SLEEPING ON COTS?

215
00:10:09.075 --> 00:10:10.586
I CAN SLEEP ANYWHERE.

216
00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.578
TAKE OUR BED. WE'LL
SLEEP ON THE COTS.

217
00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:15.914
I CAN'T SLEEP ON THESE THINGS.

218
00:10:15.949 --> 00:10:18.182
LAST TIME. GRANDMA AND GRANDPA

219
00:10:18.218 --> 00:10:20.184
SLEPT UP IN OUR ROOM.

220
00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:23.087
I WANT TO SLEEP
ON A SLEEPING BAG.

221
00:10:23.123 --> 00:10:25.101
THAT'S NOT WHAT WE DID.

222
00:10:25.125 --> 00:10:27.725
I'M PARTICULAR
ABOUT WHERE I SLEEP.

223
00:10:27.761 --> 00:10:29.227
WHAT DOES THAT MEAN?

224
00:10:29.262 --> 00:10:31.729
I'LL TELL YOU
SOMETHING ABOUT ME.

225
00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:34.866
I'LL NEVER SLEEP IN A
COMMUNIST COUNTRY.

226
00:10:35.936 --> 00:10:38.402
I'LL VISIT ONE DURING THE DAY.

227
00:10:38.438 --> 00:10:40.905
BUT I'LL NEVER SLEEP IN ONE.

228
00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.418
WELL. GOD BLESS AMERICA.

229
00:10:42.442 --> 00:10:45.276
CAN I SLEEP IN A SLEEPING BAG?

230
00:10:45.311 --> 00:10:46.410
NO. GO.

231
00:10:46.446 --> 00:10:48.413
HOW ABOUT WHAT I SAID?

232
00:10:48.448 --> 00:10:49.414
WHICH WAS?

233
00:10:49.449 --> 00:10:50.415
FORGET IT.

234
00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.417
LET'S NOT FUSS ABOUT THIS.

235
00:10:52.452 --> 00:10:54.196
WE CAN SLEEP ANYWHERE.

236
00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:57.588
GRANDMA AND
GRANDPA HAD OUR ROOM.

237
00:10:57.624 --> 00:10:59.090
THIS COT STILL SMELLS

238
00:10:59.125 --> 00:11:01.893
FROM THE DEAD
PIGEON WE FOUND IN IT.

239
00:11:01.928 --> 00:11:03.061
DARLENE.

240
00:11:03.096 --> 00:11:05.730
D.J. AND I SLEPT ON THE FLOOR.

241
00:11:05.766 --> 00:11:08.232
MOM AND DAD HAD D.J.'s BED.

242
00:11:08.268 --> 00:11:10.168
BUT IT'S TOO SMALL.

243
00:11:10.203 --> 00:11:12.715
JACKIE. YOU WERE NOT EVEN HERE.

244
00:11:12.739 --> 00:11:13.704
TEMPER. TEMPER.

245
00:11:13.739 --> 00:11:16.207
HOW COME I CAN REMEMBER IT?

246
00:11:16.242 --> 00:11:18.220
BECAUSE YOU HAVE TOTAL RECALL

247
00:11:18.244 --> 00:11:19.721
OF ALL THINGS IMAGINARY.

248
00:11:19.745 --> 00:11:21.078
GIRLS. GIRLS.

249
00:11:21.114 --> 00:11:23.314
LET'S BE LADIES. SHALL WE?

250
00:11:23.349 --> 00:11:25.817
CAN WE COME TO SOME CONCLUSION?

251
00:11:25.852 --> 00:11:27.830
I'LL GIVE YOU A CONCLUSION.

252
00:11:27.854 --> 00:11:29.832
JACKIE. SLEEP IN D.J.'s BED.

253
00:11:29.856 --> 00:11:32.167
D.J.. SLEEP IN A SLEEPING BAG!

254
00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:34.670
GIRLS. GIRLS. LET'S
BE LITTLE LADIES

255
00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:37.161
AND SLEEP IN YOUR OWN BED.

256
00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:39.797
YOU TAKE ME AND DAN'S ROOM.

257
00:11:39.832 --> 00:11:42.300
I'M GOING TO SLEEP ON THE COT.

258
00:11:42.335 --> 00:11:44.836
AND SO IS MR. FLEXIBLE.

259
00:11:44.871 --> 00:11:47.338
HOPEFULLY WE WON'T
HAVE THIS CONFUSION

260
00:11:47.373 --> 00:11:50.341
ONCE YOUR FATHER
AND I HAVE A PLACE

261
00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:51.843
RIGHT HERE IN LANFORD.

262
00:11:51.878 --> 00:11:54.245
SLEEP TIGHT. EVERYONE.

263
00:11:55.315 --> 00:11:57.282
NIGHTIE-NIGHT.

264
00:12:08.328 --> 00:12:10.472
DAN. ARE YOU SLEEPING?

265
00:12:10.496 --> 00:12:11.963
LIKE A BABY.

266
00:12:11.998 --> 00:12:14.299
THE FACT THAT IT'S 4:30 A.M.

267
00:12:14.334 --> 00:12:17.302
AND I HAVE A SPRING
IN MY PANCREAS

268
00:12:17.337 --> 00:12:20.305
ISN'T KEEPING ME AWAKE
THE LEAST LITTLE BIT.

269
00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.807
IF MY PARENTS MOVE TO LANFORD.

270
00:12:22.842 --> 00:12:25.310
I'LL BE SLEEPING ON A COT

271
00:12:25.345 --> 00:12:27.812
FOR THE REST OF MY LIFE

272
00:12:27.847 --> 00:12:31.315
BECAUSE I'LL BE IN PRISON
FOR BLOWING THEM AWAY.

273
00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:32.817
HONEY. HONEY. BE REALISTIC.

274
00:12:32.852 --> 00:12:35.820
YOU DON'T KNOW HOW TO USE A GUN.

275
00:12:35.855 --> 00:12:37.454
I'LL DO IT.

276
00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:43.828
SERIOUSLY. DAN. WHAT
ARE WE GOING TO DO?

277
00:12:43.863 --> 00:12:46.831
WELL. I'D SAY.
"LET'S SLEEP ON IT."

278
00:12:46.866 --> 00:12:48.332
BUT WHO CAN SLEEP?

279
00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:51.335
IF YOU COULD STAND
UP TO YOUR PARENTS.

280
00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.337
WE WOULDN'T BE LYING HERE.

281
00:12:53.372 --> 00:12:55.740
WHAT'S THAT SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

282
00:12:55.775 --> 00:12:58.754
I'M WARNING YOU. THAT
FIREPLACE POKER'S WITHIN REACH.

283
00:12:58.778 --> 00:13:02.112
BABY. LET'S NOT GET
INTO THIS RIGHT NOW

284
00:13:02.148 --> 00:13:05.115
BECAUSE IT'S NOT MY WARPED.
PSYCHOTIC. NEUROTIC PARENTS

285
00:13:05.151 --> 00:13:06.751
LAYING IN MY BED.

286
00:13:09.155 --> 00:13:11.622
I'M GOING TO SIT ON THE PORCH.

287
00:13:11.657 --> 00:13:12.790
HONEY. HONEY.

288
00:13:12.825 --> 00:13:15.793
HONEY. LET'S NOT DO
THIS TO EACH OTHER.

289
00:13:15.828 --> 00:13:19.297
I'M SORRY. I'M JUST ANGRY
'CAUSE I HAVEN'T SLEPT.

290
00:13:19.332 --> 00:13:22.300
WE GOT A COUPLE
HOURS LEFT TILL DAYLIGHT.

291
00:13:22.335 --> 00:13:25.436
LET'S JUST TRY TO
SALVAGE SOME SLEEP.

292
00:13:51.297 --> 00:13:52.764
[SNORTING]

293
00:13:52.799 --> 00:13:54.398
[GAGGING]

294
00:13:57.971 --> 00:13:59.370
AL?

295
00:14:01.141 --> 00:14:02.273
AL.

296
00:14:02.308 --> 00:14:03.440
OH.

297
00:14:03.476 --> 00:14:04.942
I'M JUST GOING

298
00:14:04.978 --> 00:14:06.956
TO MAKE YOUR FATHER BREAKFAST.

299
00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:09.446
HE ALWAYS GETS UP AT 4:30.

300
00:14:09.482 --> 00:14:11.402
GO BACK TO SLEEP.

301
00:14:12.118 --> 00:14:14.718
FEEL LIKE MAKING LOVE?

302
00:14:23.496 --> 00:14:28.065
I JUST WANT TO KNOW WHERE
YOU KEEP YOUR CITRUS FRUIT.

303
00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.067
THERE'S SOME
STRAWBERRY POP TARTS

304
00:14:30.102 --> 00:14:31.769
IN THE FRIDGE.

305
00:14:31.804 --> 00:14:35.506
YOUR FATHER NEEDS TO
HAVE A PIECE OF CITRUS FRUIT.

306
00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:38.142
THERE'S AN ORANGE
UNDER THE DRYER.

307
00:14:38.177 --> 00:14:41.089
DAN SHOULDN'T
SLEEP ON HIS LEFT SIDE.

308
00:14:41.113 --> 00:14:43.158
IT'S BAD FOR THE HEART.

309
00:14:43.182 --> 00:14:45.216
SO'S A RUSTY SPIKE.

310
00:14:47.787 --> 00:14:49.253
THIS IS NUTS.

311
00:14:49.288 --> 00:14:50.755
THIS IS NUTS.

312
00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.758
I GOT A NEW JOB TO START TODAY.

313
00:14:53.793 --> 00:14:55.771
I'VE GOT TO GO TO WORK. TOO.

314
00:14:55.795 --> 00:14:59.197
THEN TELL MA AND
PA KETTLE TO SHUT UP.

315
00:14:59.232 --> 00:15:02.792
WHAT ARE YOU DOING UP SO EARLY?

316
00:15:16.482 --> 00:15:18.522
YOU GOT ANY KLEENEX?

317
00:15:18.551 --> 00:15:20.751
USE DAN'S BOWLING SHIRT.

318
00:15:23.656 --> 00:15:25.990
THANKS. YOU'RE WELCOME.

319
00:15:26.026 --> 00:15:30.261
THANKS. THIS IS THE BEST
ROOM IN YOUR HOUSE.

320
00:15:30.297 --> 00:15:33.264
YEAH. 'CAUSE MOM
AND DAD AREN'T IN IT.

321
00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.766
THIS IS OUR SANCTUARY FROM THEM.

322
00:15:35.801 --> 00:15:37.268
DON'T COUNT ON IT.

323
00:15:37.303 --> 00:15:40.204
SHE'LL FIGURE OUT
SOME WAY TO GET IN.

324
00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:43.841
THEN YOU CAN STAND
UP TO HER LIKE BEFORE.

325
00:15:45.145 --> 00:15:47.123
I SAID TO YOUR GRANDMOTHER.

326
00:15:47.147 --> 00:15:49.125
"BEVERLY..." I CALL HER BEVERLY

327
00:15:49.149 --> 00:15:50.626
BECAUSE THAT'S HER NAME.

328
00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.628
I SAID. "BEVERLY. THIS YEAR

329
00:15:52.652 --> 00:15:54.130
"I'M PAYING MORE ATTENTION

330
00:15:54.154 --> 00:15:56.120
TO MY STABLE AND HORSES."

331
00:15:56.156 --> 00:15:58.622
YOU DON'T HAVE ANY
HORSES. GRANDPA.

332
00:15:58.658 --> 00:16:01.125
'CAUSE I DON'T HAVE A STABLE.

333
00:16:01.161 --> 00:16:02.638
PULL MY FINGER. KID.

334
00:16:02.662 --> 00:16:03.761
DON'T.

335
00:16:05.632 --> 00:16:07.998
I'M SORRY. WHAT WERE YOU SAYING?

336
00:16:08.034 --> 00:16:09.233
OH. I'M FINISHED.

337
00:16:09.269 --> 00:16:12.236
ARE YOU GUYS GETTING
READY FOR SCHOOL?

338
00:16:12.272 --> 00:16:15.251
YEAH. AND WE'RE
REALLY EXCITED ABOUT IT.

339
00:16:15.275 --> 00:16:16.473
THAT'S GREAT.

340
00:16:16.509 --> 00:16:19.610
THEY'RE REALLY DOING
GREAT IN SCHOOL.

341
00:16:19.646 --> 00:16:21.123
AL WAS ALWAYS CONCERNED

342
00:16:21.147 --> 00:16:22.625
WITH THE CHILDREN'S EDUCATION.

343
00:16:22.649 --> 00:16:24.114
HE WAS SOME FATHER.

344
00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:27.284
WHAT IS IT YOU
ALWAYS USED TO SAY?

345
00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:30.287
YOU CAN LEAD A HORSE TO WATER.

346
00:16:30.323 --> 00:16:33.090
BUT YOU CAN'T MAKE HIM THINK.

347
00:16:35.661 --> 00:16:38.629
YOU USED TO SAY THAT...

348
00:16:38.664 --> 00:16:40.897
AND YOU STOPPED SAYING THAT?

349
00:16:42.936 --> 00:16:44.902
HE USED TO SAY THAT.

350
00:16:44.938 --> 00:16:47.404
AND HE DOESN'T SAY IT ANYMORE.

351
00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.906
HE USED TO SAY.

352
00:16:48.942 --> 00:16:51.909
"YOU CAN LEAD A HORSE TO WATER.

353
00:16:51.945 --> 00:16:54.411
BUT YOU CAN'T MAKE HIM THINK."

354
00:16:54.447 --> 00:16:58.015
AND HE DOESN'T SAY IT ANYMORE.

355
00:16:59.319 --> 00:17:01.385
I HAVEN'T SLEPT.

356
00:17:07.527 --> 00:17:09.993
HOW DID WE GROW UP NORMAL?

357
00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:12.996
'CAUSE YOU HAD ME
TO SAVE YOUR BUTT.

358
00:17:13.032 --> 00:17:17.000
I RECALL I DID A LITTLE
BUTT-SAVING FOR YOU. TOO.

359
00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:18.502
WE'RE ONLY SANE TODAY

360
00:17:18.538 --> 00:17:21.505
BECAUSE WE KEPT
EACH OTHER THAT WAY.

361
00:17:21.541 --> 00:17:23.018
WE PROTECTED EACH OTHER

362
00:17:23.042 --> 00:17:25.509
FROM MR. AND MRS.
TOTAL INSANITY.

363
00:17:25.545 --> 00:17:28.512
YEAH. LIKE WHEN YOU
WERE IN EIGHTH GRADE

364
00:17:28.548 --> 00:17:30.781
AND YOU DATED THAT
40-YEAR-OLD GUY.

365
00:17:30.817 --> 00:17:32.983
HE WAS NOT 40.

366
00:17:33.019 --> 00:17:36.487
HE WAS THE ONLY GUY
AT YOUR FRESHMAN DANCE

367
00:17:36.523 --> 00:17:37.988
WEARING A TOUPEE.

368
00:17:38.024 --> 00:17:40.924
I TOLD MOM HE WAS YOUR TUTOR.

369
00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.494
AND I TAUGHT HIM MORE.

370
00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:45.596
THAT'S THE WAY IT GOES.

371
00:17:45.632 --> 00:17:48.599
THE BOTTOM LINE IS
THAT MOM AND DAD

372
00:17:48.635 --> 00:17:50.601
ARE JUST SO OUT THERE.

373
00:17:50.637 --> 00:17:53.604
WELL. YOU KNOW. IT'S
NOT ALL THEIR FAULT.

374
00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:56.607
WE SHOULD SHOW THEM
A LITTLE COMPASSION.

375
00:17:56.643 --> 00:17:58.621
WELL. HERE WE GO AGAIN.

376
00:17:58.645 --> 00:18:01.156
CHECK IN YOUR
BACKBONE AT THE DOOR.

377
00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:04.649
WELL. FINE. YOU BLAME
YOUR WHOLE LIFE ON THEM.

378
00:18:04.684 --> 00:18:07.151
ROSEANNE. YOU TURN INTO A ROBOT

379
00:18:07.186 --> 00:18:10.154
EVERY TIME MOM AND
DAD COME AROUND.

380
00:18:10.189 --> 00:18:12.489
AND I'M SICK OF IT.

381
00:18:12.525 --> 00:18:14.992
PEOPLE WHO LIVE IN
COCKROACH-INFESTED APARTMENTS

382
00:18:15.028 --> 00:18:16.560
SHOULD NOT THROW STONES.

383
00:18:16.596 --> 00:18:19.563
YOU ALWAYS HAVE TO
GET YOUR OWN WAY.

384
00:18:19.599 --> 00:18:21.665
IT HAS TO BE MY WAY

385
00:18:21.701 --> 00:18:23.667
WHEN YOU'RE IN MY BATHROOM

386
00:18:23.702 --> 00:18:26.670
AFTER MY PARENTS
CAME OVER TO MY HOUSE...

387
00:18:26.705 --> 00:18:28.183
NOW THEY'RE <i>YOUR</i> PARENTS!

388
00:18:28.207 --> 00:18:31.175
IF YOU WANT THEM.
FINE. YOU HAVE THEM!

389
00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.744
TELL ME WHEN IT'S
THEIR ANNIVERSARY

390
00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:36.747
AND YOU LET THEM
STAY AT YOUR HOUSE

391
00:18:36.782 --> 00:18:38.249
AND DECIMATE YOUR FAMILY.

392
00:18:38.284 --> 00:18:39.616
WHICH YOU DON'T HAVE

393
00:18:39.652 --> 00:18:42.453
BECAUSE YOU CAN'T
CONCENTRATE ON NOTHING LONGER

394
00:18:42.488 --> 00:18:44.888
THAN IT TAKES TO CHUG A BEER.

395
00:18:44.924 --> 00:18:47.391
DON'T GIVE ME THAT WOUNDED LOOK

396
00:18:47.427 --> 00:18:50.494
BECAUSE THAT ONLY
WORKS ON GUYS NAMED MIKE.

397
00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:52.129
VERY DRAMATIC. ROSEANNE.

398
00:18:52.165 --> 00:18:56.867
OH. SO NOW YOU'RE NOT
GOING TO TALK TO ME.

399
00:18:58.304 --> 00:19:01.271
GOD. WOULD I LOVE
TO THROW A HAMMER

400
00:19:01.307 --> 00:19:03.273
THROUGH A PLATE GLASS WINDOW.

401
00:19:03.309 --> 00:19:06.288
HER MAJESTY'S NOT
SPEAKING TO ANYBODY TODAY.

402
00:19:06.312 --> 00:19:08.912
HEY. JACKIE. WHO EVEN ASKED YOU?

403
00:19:08.948 --> 00:19:11.227
I'M A PART OF THIS FAMILY.

404
00:19:11.251 --> 00:19:13.584
YEAH. WHEN YOUR HAMPER'S FULL.

405
00:19:13.620 --> 00:19:16.799
I'VE BEEN IN THIS FAMILY
LONGER THAN YOU.

406
00:19:16.823 --> 00:19:19.957
BOY. THAT'S SOMETHING
TO BE PROUD OF.

407
00:19:20.894 --> 00:19:24.361
I SAW A WHOLE THING
ABOUT THIS ON<i> OPRAH.</i>

408
00:19:24.397 --> 00:19:26.163
AND WE'RE JUST LIKE THAT.

409
00:19:26.198 --> 00:19:30.334
WE ARE A DYSFUNCTIONAL FAMILY!

410
00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.336
AAH!

411
00:19:32.371 --> 00:19:33.470
AAH!

412
00:19:38.711 --> 00:19:41.112
THERE. THAT WILL NEVER COME OUT.

413
00:19:41.147 --> 00:19:44.126
I LEARNED THAT WHILE
I WAS A PARATROOPER.

414
00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:48.252
I WONDER HOW MANY TIMES
HE LANDED ON HIS HEAD.

415
00:19:49.155 --> 00:19:50.121
THANKS. GRAMPS.

416
00:19:50.156 --> 00:19:52.123
BYE. GRAM.

417
00:19:52.158 --> 00:19:53.124
BYE. BECKY.

418
00:19:53.159 --> 00:19:54.125
GOODBYE. DEAR.

419
00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:58.395
GRANDPA SAID HE'D BUY
ME A HORSE NEXT YEAR.

420
00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:01.765
YEAH. WELL. GRANDPA'S
SADDLE'S ON TOO TIGHT.

421
00:20:01.801 --> 00:20:03.400
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

422
00:20:03.436 --> 00:20:05.702
MAKING BREAKFAST FOR MY KIDS.

423
00:20:05.738 --> 00:20:07.971
I ALREADY MADE THEM BREAKFAST.

424
00:20:08.007 --> 00:20:10.040
GO TO SCHOOL. THEN.

425
00:20:10.076 --> 00:20:11.141
BYE.

426
00:20:11.177 --> 00:20:12.142
BYE. KIDS.

427
00:20:12.178 --> 00:20:13.644
SHE MADE THEM BREAKFAST.

428
00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.746
CEREAL WITH
CHOCOLATE CHIP COOKIES.

429
00:20:15.782 --> 00:20:17.760
YOUR FATHER GAVE THEM COOKIES.

430
00:20:17.784 --> 00:20:19.817
EATING THEM NOW OR LATER.

431
00:20:19.852 --> 00:20:21.451
WHAT'S THE DIFFERENCE?

432
00:20:21.487 --> 00:20:23.954
YOU WANT TO KNOW THE DIFFERENCE?

433
00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:27.457
THE DIFFERENCE IS YOU
SHOW UP AT MY DOOR

434
00:20:27.493 --> 00:20:28.458
UNANNOUNCED. UNINVITED.

435
00:20:28.494 --> 00:20:31.461
YOU JUST WORK
EVERYBODY UP INTO A FRENZY

436
00:20:31.497 --> 00:20:34.531
UNTIL WE'RE READY
TO KILL EACH OTHER!

437
00:20:34.567 --> 00:20:36.545
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

438
00:20:36.569 --> 00:20:37.913
WE'RE HAVING BREAKFAST.

439
00:20:37.937 --> 00:20:39.836
IF YOU MOVE TO LANFORD.

440
00:20:39.872 --> 00:20:43.441
YOU'LL HAVE TO MOVE TO
THE OTHER SIDE OF TOWN.

441
00:20:43.476 --> 00:20:45.509
I CAN'T TAKE THIS FOREVER.

442
00:20:45.545 --> 00:20:47.644
WHO'S MOVING TO LANFORD?

443
00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:48.779
YOU ARE.

444
00:20:48.815 --> 00:20:50.614
YOU SAID SO LAST NIGHT.

445
00:20:50.650 --> 00:20:53.116
WE'RE NEVER GOING
TO MOVE INTO LANFORD.

446
00:20:53.152 --> 00:20:54.630
WE WERE JUST THINKING.

447
00:20:54.654 --> 00:20:56.131
WE WERE JUST TALKING.

448
00:20:56.155 --> 00:20:59.556
WHY DO YOU TAKE
EVERYTHING SO SERIOUSLY?

449
00:20:59.592 --> 00:21:01.070
SO YOU'RE NOT MOVING?

450
00:21:01.094 --> 00:21:03.627
NO. IN FACT. WE'VE GOT TO GO.

451
00:21:03.663 --> 00:21:06.129
WE'RE GOING TO
SEE COUSIN SIDNEY.

452
00:21:06.165 --> 00:21:07.631
HE HAD GUM SURGERY.

453
00:21:07.667 --> 00:21:10.868
I'M GOING TO BUY HIM
SOME ROCK CANDY.

454
00:21:13.606 --> 00:21:17.374
WELL. IT'S A SHAME YOU
COULDN'T HAVE STAYED LONGER.

455
00:21:18.678 --> 00:21:21.311
DAN. DO YOU REALLY MEAN THAT?

456
00:21:21.347 --> 00:21:23.313
HEY. IF YOU DON'T THINK

457
00:21:23.349 --> 00:21:25.315
YOUR LEAVING WILL
AFFECT EVERYBODY.

458
00:21:25.351 --> 00:21:26.683
YOU'RE CRAZY.

459
00:21:26.719 --> 00:21:28.185
OH. THAT'S SO SWEET.

460
00:21:28.221 --> 00:21:30.187
AL. DID YOU HEAR THAT?

461
00:21:30.223 --> 00:21:33.924
YEAH. I'D GIVE HIM A BIG KISS...

462
00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:35.003
OH...

463
00:21:35.027 --> 00:21:36.694
IF I LIKED BOYS.

464
00:21:42.669 --> 00:21:45.636
OH. MOM. I'M REALLY
GOING TO MISS YOU.

465
00:21:45.672 --> 00:21:46.637
ME. TOO.

466
00:21:46.673 --> 00:21:48.872
OH...

467
00:21:52.512 --> 00:21:54.911
THIS HAS BEEN A GREAT VISIT.

468
00:21:54.947 --> 00:21:58.515
OH. THIS HAS BEEN
A WONDERFUL VISIT.

469
00:21:58.551 --> 00:22:00.985
LET ME DO IT AGAIN.

470
00:22:11.029 --> 00:22:13.007
DID YOU WASH YOUR HANDS?

471
00:22:13.031 --> 00:22:14.042
GROW UP!

472
00:22:14.066 --> 00:22:16.933
YOU'RE CRANKY 'CAUSE MOMMY
AND DADDY SAID GOODBYE.

473
00:22:16.969 --> 00:22:18.435
NO. I'M NOT.

474
00:22:18.471 --> 00:22:21.438
OH. ADMIT IT. I
GET THE SAME WAY.

475
00:22:21.474 --> 00:22:23.940
NO MATTER HOW OLD YOU ARE.

476
00:22:23.976 --> 00:22:26.943
YOU NEVER LIKE TO
HEAR THEM SAY GOODBYE.

477
00:22:26.979 --> 00:22:29.446
YEAH. I GUESS IT'S THAT FEAR

478
00:22:29.482 --> 00:22:32.449
THAT YOU MIGHT
NEVER SEE THEM AGAIN.

479
00:22:32.485 --> 00:22:34.585
BABY. YOU'LL SEE THEM AGAIN.

480
00:22:36.989 --> 00:22:39.956
I KNOW. AND THE SICK THING IS

481
00:22:39.992 --> 00:22:42.459
THAT I KIND OF MISS THEM.

482
00:22:42.495 --> 00:22:44.094
I KIND OF DON'T.

483
00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:48.465
DAN?

484
00:22:48.501 --> 00:22:50.100
WHATY?

485
00:22:50.135 --> 00:22:52.168
PULL MY FINGER.

486
00:23:01.881 --> 00:23:04.080
AAH!

487
00:23:04.116 --> 00:23:05.849
AAH!

488
00:23:18.464 --> 00:23:19.429
HI.

489
00:23:19.465 --> 00:23:20.931
RIGHT. HERE'S THE DEAL.

490
00:23:20.967 --> 00:23:22.933
I'LL GET THE CHECKBOOK OUT.

491
